articles.text_before:
1. The driving licence provided for in Article 1 shall authorise the driving of power-driven vehicles in the categories defined hereunder. It may be issued from the minimum age indicated for each category. A 'power-driven vehicle' means any self-propelled vehicle running on a road under its own power, other than a rail-borne vehicle.
(a) Category AM: two-wheel or three-wheel vehicles with a maximum design speed of not more than 45 km/h, and light quadricycles;
(b) Category A1: motorcycles with a cylinder capacity not exceeding 125 cm3, of a power not exceeding 11 kW and with a power/weight ratio not exceeding 0,1 kW/kg;
(c) Category A2: motorcycles of a power not exceeding 35 kW and with a power/weight ratio not exceeding 0,2 kW/kg;
(d) Category A: motorcycles;
(e) Category B: motor vehicles with a maximum authorised mass not exceeding 3 500 kg and designed and constructed for the carriage of no more than eight passengers in addition to the driver;
(f) Category BE: combinations of vehicles where the tractor vehicle is in category B and the trailer has a maximum authorised mass not exceeding 3 500 kg;
(g) Category C1: motor vehicles other than those in categories D1 or D, the maximum authorised mass of which exceeds 3 500 kg but not more than 7 500 kg;
(h) Category C1E: without prejudice to type-approval rules for the vehicles concerned, combinations of vehicles where the tractor vehicle is in category C1;
(i) Category C: motor vehicles other than those in categories D1 or D, the maximum authorised mass of which exceeds 3 500 kg;
(j) Category CE: without prejudice to type-approval rules for the vehicles concerned, combinations of vehicles where the tractor vehicle is in category C;
(k) Category D1: motor vehicles designed and constructed for the carriage of no more than 16 passengers in addition to the driver and with a maximum length not exceeding 8 m;
(l) Category D1E: without prejudice to type-approval rules for the vehicles concerned, combinations of vehicles where the tractor vehicle is in category D1;
(m) Category D: motor vehicles designed and constructed for the carriage of more than eight passengers in addition to the driver;
(n) Category DE: without prejudice to type-approval rules for the vehicles concerned, combinations of vehicles where the tractor vehicle is in category D.

